      '@id': 'https://cassiancreed.com/court-calendar#breadcrumb',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://cassiancreed.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'True Crime Court Calendar', item: 'https://cassiancreed.com/court-calendar' },
      ],
    },
    {
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      '@id': 'https://cassiancreed.com/court-calendar#faq',
      mainEntity: [
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'When does the Lindsay Clancy trial start?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'It is underway. Jury selection ran July 20 to July 23, 2026, in Plymouth County Superior Court before Judge William F. Sullivan, and an 18-juror panel was seated — 12 jurors and 6 alternates. Opening statements begin Monday, July 27, 2026, and prosecutors are expected to call the children’s father as their first witness. Attorneys estimate at least six weeks. Prosecutors dropped three duplicative strangulation counts on July 9, leaving three counts of first-degree murder. She has pleaded not guilty and is presumed innocent.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Was Colt Gray sentenced?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Not yet. He pleaded guilty on July 24, 2026, to all 55 counts in the Apalachee High School shooting in a non-negotiated plea, meaning no sentence was agreed in advance. Chief Judge Nicholas Primm accepted the plea and began the sentencing hearing the same day before adjourning it to Monday, July 27, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. Eastern. The minimum available sentence is life with the possibility of parole; the maximum is life without parole.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is the next court date for Dianne Curry Peck?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'A pretrial conference is set for Monday, August 31, 2026, in Bristol County Superior Court in Fall River. Two outlets that reviewed the court file report that date; one broadcast report instead said December, and we are flagging that disagreement rather than picking quietly. She was indicted on one count of murder, pleaded not guilty, and was released on $100,000 surety with $10,000 cash posted. No trial date has been set.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Does Brooke George have a trial date?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. There is no publicly verified court date. She is reported to be detained pending proceedings, but the details of the allegation come from an advocacy group rather than from UAE authorities or any court, and no charge has been confirmed on the public record.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is Karmelo Anthony still facing an upcoming court date?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes — two. A hearing on his motion to recuse the trial judge is set for Wednesday, August 19, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. Central in the 494th District Court in Collin County, before Senior Judge Sid L. Harle. A hearing on his motion for a new trial is set for Thursday, August 20, 2026, with the courtroom and presiding judge not yet assigned. He was convicted of murder on June 9, 2026, sentenced to 35 years, and filed a notice of appeal the next day.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is Rex Heuermann still going to trial?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. That case is over. It concluded with a guilty plea in April 2026 and sentencing in June 2026. There is no upcoming court date.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Can these dates change?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes, and they often do. Hearings get continued, trials get pushed, and courts reschedule with little notice. Treat every date here as the best current information, not a promise.' } },
        { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How are these dates verified?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Each one traces to a court filing, a prosecutor\'s office, a state agency record, or courtroom reporting, and each card names its source and the date we last checked it.' } },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---
<Base
  title="True Crime Court Calendar: Trial Dates & Hearings 2026"
  description="Track verified 2026 true-crime trial dates, hearings, sentencing proceedings, and appeals, including Lindsay Clancy, Dianne Curry Peck, and other major cases."
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Court Calendar</p>
    <h1>True Crime Court Calendar: Trial Dates &amp; Hearings 2026</h1>
    <p class="cal-answer">
      Colt Gray pleaded guilty <strong>July 24</strong> to all 55 counts in the Apalachee High School shooting; his sentencing hearing resumes <strong>Monday, July 27</strong> in Barrow County, and his father Colin Gray is sentenced <strong>July 30</strong>. Opening statements in Lindsay Clancy&rsquo;s murder trial begin <strong>Monday, July 27</strong> in Plymouth County, before a jury seated July 23. Karmelo Anthony has his first post-conviction hearings <strong>August 19 and 20</strong> in Collin County, Texas. Dianne Curry Peck&rsquo;s pretrial conference is set for <strong>August 31</strong> in Fall River, Yvonne &ldquo;Missy&rdquo; Woods is sentenced <strong>September 8</strong> in Jefferson County, Colorado, and Larry Millete is sentenced <strong>September 29</strong> in Chula Vista.
    </p>
    <p class="cal-fresh">
      <strong>Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED}.</strong> Court dates move. Every entry below is checked against the public record, and each one carries its source. Confirm with the court before you travel.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="next-dates">
    <h2 id="next-dates">Next Court Dates</h2>
    <p class="cal-sub">Everything currently on a calendar, in date order.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      {nextDates.map((e) => (
        <article class="card" id={e.id}>
          <p class="card__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
          <h3 class="card__case">{e.case}</h3>
          <p class="card__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time></p>
          <p class="card__court">{e.court}</p>
          <p class="card__status"><span class="card__k">Status</span> {e.status}</p>
          <p class="card__detail">{e.detail}</p>
          <p class="card__meta">
            <span class="card__verified">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED}</span>
            <span class="card__change">All dates are subject to change by the court.</span>
          </p>
          <p class="card__src">
            <span class="card__k">Source</span>
            <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a>
            <span class="card__srctype">{e.srcType}</span>
          </p>
          <p class="card__links">
            {e.link ? (
              <a class="card__read" href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a>
            ) : (
              <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>
            )}
            {e.link2 && <a class="card__read" href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>}
            <a class="card__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a>
          </p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec">
    <div class="capture-cta" aria-label="Stay current on this court calendar and get the free case-reading guide">
      <p class="capture-cta__eyebrow">Came here for a date?</p>
      <h2 class="capture-cta__head">We&rsquo;ll keep you current on the calendar.</h2>
      <p class="capture-cta__body">
        Court dates move &mdash; and so does what a hearing actually settles. We&rsquo;ll send you <em>How to Read a Case Like the Court Does</em> &mdash; a plain-language framework for weighing evidence instead of guessing, and what a verdict really settles (and what it doesn&rsquo;t) &mdash; plus calendar updates when dates change. No weekly blast; unsubscribe anytime.
      </p>
      <a class="capture-cta__btn" href="https://cassiancreed.beehiiv.com/subscribe?utm_source=website&utm_medium=court_calendar&utm_campaign=lm_case_how-to-read-a-case">
        Get the guide &amp; date updates
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="upcoming-trials">
    <h2 id="upcoming-trials">Upcoming Trials</h2>
    {byGroup('trials').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} {e.link2 && <a href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="hearings">
    <h2 id="hearings">Hearings &amp; Pretrial</h2>
    {byGroup('hearings').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">
          {e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>}
          <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="sentencing">
    <h2 id="sentencing">Sentencing &amp; Appeals</h2>
    {byGroup('sentencing').map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.proceeding}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when"><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time> &middot; {e.court}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a></p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} {e.link2 && <a href={e.link2}>{e.linkText2} &rarr;</a>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
    {appeals.map((e) => (
      <div class="row">
        <p class="row__type">{e.type || 'Post-conviction motions'}</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when">{e.when || 'No hearing date publicly confirmed'} &middot; {e.where}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__note">{e.note}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a> ({e.srcType})</p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="unconfirmed">
    <h2 id="unconfirmed">Dates Not Yet Confirmed</h2>
    <p class="cal-sub">These cases are active, but no date is on a public calendar. We do not publish a date until we can point to where it came from.</p>
    {unconfirmed.map((e) => (
      <div class="row row--muted">
        <p class="row__type">No date set</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when">{e.where}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__note">{e.note}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; subject to change by the court &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a> ({e.srcType})</p>
        <p class="row__links">
          {e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>}
          <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="completed">
    <h2 id="completed">Recently Completed</h2>
    {completed.map((e) => (
      <div class="row row--done">
        <p class="row__type">Concluded</p>
        <h3 class="row__case">{e.case}</h3>
        <p class="row__when">{e.where}</p>
        <p class="row__status">{e.status}</p>
        <p class="row__note">{e.note}</p>
        <p class="row__meta">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED} &middot; Source: <a href={e.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{e.srcLabel}</a> ({e.srcType})</p>
        <p class="row__links">{e.link ? <a href={e.link}>{e.linkText} &rarr;</a> : <span class="card__soon">Our case file on this is in progress.</span>} <a class="row__help" href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a></p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="case-by-case">
    <h2 id="case-by-case">Case-by-Case Schedule</h2>
    <div class="cal-scroll">
      <table class="cal-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Case</th>
            <th scope="col">Proceeding</th>
            <th scope="col">Date</th>
            <th scope="col">Court</th>
            <th scope="col">Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {nextDates.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="t-case">{e.case}</td>
              <td>{e.proceeding}</td>
              <td><time datetime={e.dateISO}>{e.dateText}</time></td>
              <td>{e.court}</td>
              <td class="t-status">{e.status}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          {appeals.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="t-case">{e.case}</td>
              <td>{e.type || 'Post-conviction motions'}</td>
              <td class="t-none">No date set</td>
              <td>{e.where}</td>
              <td class="t-status">{e.status}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          {unconfirmed.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="t-case">{e.case}</td>
              <td class="t-none">&mdash;</td>
              <td class="t-none">No date set</td>
              <td>{e.where}</td>
              <td class="t-status">{e.status}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          {completed.map((e) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="t-case">{e.case}</td>
              <td>Concluded</td>
              <td class="t-none">No upcoming date</td>
              <td>{e.where}</td>
              <td class="t-status">{e.status}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="cal-note evidence">Last verified: {LAST_VERIFIED}. All dates are subject to change by the court.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="how-we-verify">
    <h2 id="how-we-verify">How We Verify Court Dates</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A wrong date is not a small mistake. It sends a victim's family to an empty courtroom, and it puts a scheduled proceeding in a defendant's name that may not exist. So we hold every line on this page to the same rule.</p>
      <p>Cassian Creed maintains this Neural Edge Publishing calendar as a verification index, not a source of record: every published date must trace to a court, prosecutor, state agency, or identified courtroom report. When a date cannot be tied to a public source, Neural Edge Publishing leaves it unconfirmed rather than turning an expectation into a scheduled proceeding.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>The source is never us.</strong> Each date traces to a court filing, a prosecutor's office, a state agency record, or a reporter who was in the room. We do not cite our own articles as the source for a date.</li>
        <li><strong>We name the source type.</strong> A district attorney's announcement and a news report are not the same thing, so we label which one you are looking at.</li>
        <li><strong>No date, no entry.</strong> If a case is active but nothing is scheduled, it goes in <a href="#unconfirmed">Dates Not Yet Confirmed</a> and stays there. We would rather say "we don't know" than guess.</li>
        <li><strong>We re-check before we publish, and we date the check.</strong> Every card carries the date it was last verified.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal status is stated exactly.</strong> Charged is not convicted. A plea is not a verdict. An appeal is not a retrial.</li>
        <li><strong>A press conference is not a hearing.</strong> Briefings, filing deadlines, and announcements do not go on the calendar. Only proceedings a court has actually set do.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Even so: courts continue courts. If you plan to attend, call the clerk's office first.</p>
      <p>Want to feel why seating twelve takes days? <a href="/voir-dire-simulator/">Play our free Voir Dire Simulator</a> &mdash; question the pool, argue cause, and try to survive a Batson challenge.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec" aria-labelledby="faq">
    <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="prose faq">
      <h3>When does the Lindsay Clancy trial start?</h3>
      <p>It is underway. Jury selection ran July 20 to July 23, 2026, in Plymouth County Superior Court before Judge William F. Sullivan, and an 18-juror panel was seated — 12 jurors and 6 alternates. Opening statements begin Monday, July 27, 2026, and prosecutors are expected to call the children’s father as their first witness. Attorneys estimate at least six weeks. Prosecutors dropped three duplicative strangulation counts on July 9, leaving three counts of first-degree murder. She has pleaded not guilty and is presumed innocent.</p>

      <h3>Was Colt Gray sentenced?</h3>
      <p>Not yet. He pleaded guilty on July 24, 2026, to all 55 counts in the Apalachee High School shooting in a non-negotiated plea, meaning no sentence was agreed in advance. Chief Judge Nicholas Primm accepted the plea and began the sentencing hearing the same day before adjourning it to Monday, July 27, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. Eastern. The minimum available sentence is life with the possibility of parole; the maximum is life without parole.</p>

      <h3>What is the next court date for Dianne Curry Peck?</h3>
      <p>A pretrial conference is set for Monday, August 31, 2026, in Bristol County Superior Court in Fall River. Two outlets that reviewed the court file report that date; one broadcast report instead said December, and we are flagging that disagreement rather than picking quietly. She was indicted on one count of murder, pleaded not guilty, and was released on $100,000 surety with $10,000 cash posted. No trial date has been set.</p>

      <h3>Does Brooke George have a trial date?</h3>
      <p>No. There is no publicly verified court date. She is reported to be detained pending proceedings, but the details of the allegation come from an advocacy group rather than from UAE authorities or any court, and no charge has been confirmed on the public record.</p>

      <h3>Is Karmelo Anthony still facing an upcoming court date?</h3>
      <p>Yes — two. A hearing on his motion to recuse the trial judge is set for Wednesday, August 19, 2026, at 9:00 a.m. Central in the 494th District Court in Collin County, before Senior Judge Sid L. Harle. A hearing on his motion for a new trial is set for Thursday, August 20, 2026, with the courtroom and presiding judge not yet assigned. He was convicted of murder on June 9, 2026, sentenced to 35 years, and filed a notice of appeal the next day.</p>

      <h3>Is Rex Heuermann still going to trial?</h3>
      <p>No. That case is over. It concluded with a guilty plea in April 2026 and sentencing in June 2026. There is no upcoming court date.</p>

      <h3>Can these dates change?</h3>
      <p>Yes, and they often do. Hearings get continued, trials get pushed, and courts reschedule with little notice. Treat every date here as the best current information, not a promise.</p>

      <h3>How are these dates verified?</h3>
      <p>Each one traces to a court filing, a prosecutor's office, a state agency record, or courtroom reporting, and each card names its source and the date we last checked it. See <a href="#how-we-verify">How We Verify Court Dates</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap cal-sec">
    <p class="cal-help">
      True crime is about real people. If a case on this page touches something in your own life, our <a href="/support/">Victim &amp; Reader Resources</a> page lists free, confidential help.
    </p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .capture-cta{background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:10px;padding:20px}
    .capture-cta__eyebrow{margin:0 0 6px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
    .capture-cta__head{margin:0 0 10px;font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.35rem;line-height:1.2;color:var(--ink)}
    .capture-cta__body{margin:0 0 16px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;max-width:60ch}
    .capture-cta__btn{display:inline-block;padding:11px 18px;border:1px solid var(--accent);border-radius:8px;background:var(--accent);color:var(--bg-2);font-family:var(--mono);font-size:.9rem;text-decoration:none}
    .capture-cta__btn:hover{background:var(--bg-2);color:var(--accent)}
    .cal-answer{font-size:19px;color:var(--ink);max-width:68ch;margin:18px 0 0;line-height:1.6}
    .cal-answer strong{color:var(--accent)}
    .cal-fresh{font-size:15px;color:var(--ink-2);max-width:68ch;margin:14px 0 0}
    .cal-fresh strong{color:var(--ink)}
    .cal-sec{margin:44px auto 0}
    .cal-sec h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:26px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .cal-sub{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:15px;margin:0 0 18px;max-width:66ch}
    .cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:16px;margin-top:18px}
    .card{background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:10px;padding:20px}
    .card__type,.row__type{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin:0 0 8px}
    .card__case,.row__case{font-family:var(--serif);font-size:21px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--ink)}
    .card__when{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:15px;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 4px}
    .card__court,.row__when{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:14px;margin:0 0 12px}
    .card__status,.row__status{font-size:15px;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.5}
    .card__detail,.row__note{font-size:14px;color:var(--ink-2);margin:0 0 12px;line-height:1.5}
    .card__k{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);display:block;margin-bottom:2px}
    .card__meta{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;margin:0 0 10px}
    .card__verified,.card__change,.row__meta{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--ink-3);letter-spacing:.03em}
    .card__src{font-size:13px;margin:0 0 12px}
    .card__src a,.row__meta a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:2px}
    .card__srctype{display:block;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--ink-3);margin-top:3px}
    .card__links,.row__links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:14px;align-items:center;margin:0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .card__read,.row__links a{color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none;font-size:14px}
    .card__read:hover,.row__links a:hover{text-decoration:underline}
    .card__help,.row__help{color:var(--ink-2)!important;font-size:13px}
    .card__soon{color:var(--ink-3);font-size:13px}
    .row{padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .row:last-child{border-bottom:0}
    .row--muted .row__type{color:var(--ink-3)}
    .row--done .row__type{color:#5fae7e}
    .row__meta{display:block;margin:0 0 10px}
    .cal-scroll{overflow-x:auto;margin:18px 0 12px;background:var(--bg-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px}
